{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Asymptotics"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.maxContact_d2_exponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.maxContact_d2_exponent","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactHasBulk.lean#L190-L196","doc":"The `d = 2` case, `θ = 1/2`, giving per-nucleon exponent `1/2`. Recorded as a cross-check that\nthe mechanism is dimensional bookkeeping and not a coincidence at 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.maxContact_d3_eq_semf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.maxContact_d3_eq_semf","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactHasBulk.lean#L179-L188","doc":"**At `d = 3` the exponent is `1/3` — the SEMF surface exponent.** The packing literature gives\n`θ = 2/3` for congruent spheres in 3-space (elementary boundary scaling `A_surf ∼ A^((d−1)/d)` gives `θ = 2/3` for a compact\nthree-dimensional cluster; this is that value instantiated, so the one geometric input is visible\nin the statement rather than buried. No constant from the packing literature is used — none is\nheld in `library/` or registered in `references.ts`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.maxContact_exponent_eq_inv_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.maxContact_exponent_eq_inv_dim","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactHasBulk.lean#L168-L177","doc":"**`p = 1/d`, derived rather than assumed.** A compact `d`-dimensional packing has boundary of\ndimension `d − 1`, so its contact count's sublinear exponent is `θ = (d−1)/d`; substituting into\n`subAffine_perNucleon` gives per-nucleon exponent `1 − θ = 1/d`. `SurfaceExponentIsDimension`\n*hypothesised* this reading. It is NOT thereby derived: `CoordinationSurfaceDeficit` already had\n`p = 1/3` from `A_surf = c·A^(2/3)`, which is the same geometric import written the other way\nround. What changes is which of the two is the primitive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.subAffine_hasBulk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.subAffine_hasBulk","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactHasBulk.lean#L157-L164","doc":"**The surface count a sub-affine bond count implies has a bulk.** Writing the correction as\n`CoordinationSurfaceDeficit`'s deficit `(k − k')·A_surf/2 = c·A^θ` gives\n`A_surf = (2c/(k − k'))·A^θ`, which satisfies `HasBulk` for `0 < θ < 1`. So the sub-affine shape\npasses the criterion that the chain and the deltahedron each failed — the only shape considered\nin this corpus that does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.subAffine_ne_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.subAffine_ne_affine","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactHasBulk.lean#L146-L155","doc":"**The sub-affine shape escapes the affine exclusion.** For `0 < θ < 1` its per-nucleon\nexponent `1 − θ` is not `1`, so by `perNucleonExp_exponent_inj` it differs at some `A` from the\n`p = 1` law every affine bond count produces. This is the first shape in the corpus that does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.subAffine_perNucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.subAffine_perNucleon","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactHasBulk.lean#L135-L144","doc":"**The sub-affine per-nucleon law has exponent `1 − θ`.** The per-nucleon exponent is the\ncomplement of the count's sublinear exponent — this is the whole mechanism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.subAffineBondCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactHasBulk.subAffineBondCount","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactHasBulk.lean#L131-L133","doc":"The **sub-affine** bond count: a linear bulk term minus a sublinear correction,\n`M(A) = κ·A − c·A^θ`. This is the shape of a maximum-contact packing's contact number. ","signatureChunk":0}]}